LimitDrawer shows who writes each limit and what to send them as a file drawer: one manila folder per limit-writer, its tab at its own cut position so no tab hides another, what the limit sets on the folder, a clipped white slip listing what to send, and a navy index label naming where it applies.

- On the site: a `table` block with `"look": "limit-drawer"` (renderer `assets/src/blocks/look-limit-drawer.js`); ind-process.1 "Who writes your limit, and what to send". Origin: pass 12 concept `design-system/inspiration/gemini/216-p12-ind-process-limits.png` (weak; idea only: its overlapping tabs, codes, slogan and contact line are not copied).
- Fields: `cols` [who writes the limit, what it sets, what to send, where it applies], `rows` (cells strings or `{t, link}`). The tab shows the row number and the writer up to its first number ("ASTM D1193-24"), else its first word ("Recipe"). What to send splits at ";" into slip lines.
- Markup: `div.aq-limit-drawer` → `ol.__list` of `li.__f` (`--i`, `--cut` 0/1/2): `span.__tab` (aria-hidden), `div.__body` (`data-theme="light"`: `h3.__who`, `p.__k` + `p.__sets`, `div.__slip` with `span.__clip`, `p.__sk`, `ul.__send`, then `a.__label` with `span.__lk`, or `p.__label` without a link), then `div.__front` with `span.__pull` (the drawer's rail, aria-hidden).
- Desktop: three folders to a row; tab cuts step left, middle, right along each row (the right cut is right-aligned), 30 px tabs, at least a third of the folder wide. Every second folder is a shade deeper (`limestone` mixed with `on-limestone`). Slips sit at a slight angle; pointing at or focusing into a folder lifts its tab and draws the slip a step out (240 ms, cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1)).
- Tokens: `limestone` folders with `on-limestone` text and `on-limestone-muted` mono labels, `surface-raised` slip with `line` edge and `flow` kicker and dashes, `navy` label with `on-navy`. No shadows.
- **Phones and tablets** (≤ 860 px): one folder per row. With PhoneKit on (S11 accordion) the tabs keep their stepped cuts, each folder closes to its tab and a 48 px head (`button.__head`: the writer, a chevron) and one is open at a time (`__more` is the body; `display: contents` on desktop); height at 375 1,237 px. Without script every folder is open, its tab on the left (up to 80 % wide), writer 19/25, what it sets and the slip lines 14/21, the slip upright, the label a full-width row link at least 48 px with the arrow at the right. Height at 375: 2,410 px (the proof-folders render it replaced was 3,618).
- Not for evidence with proof sheets and stamps (use ProofFolders) or for more than about nine writers.

## Motion

Ported from Subframe Motion "Folder open animation" (archive-folder), MIT: folders rise out of the drawer row by row, left to right, each tab a beat before its body, then the slip slides up out of the folder to its resting angle (480 ms, the document curve). Hover lift in CSS. Reduced motion: the drawer as drawn.
